<title>SPAIN: Spain's unemployment fell to 21.66 pct Dec/Feb.</title>
<headline>Spain's unemployment fell to 21.66 pct Dec/Feb.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish unemployment from December 1996 to February 1997 fell 0.21 points to 21.66 percent, the National Statistics Institute INE said on Friday.</p>
<p>The data is based on the INE survey, completed on a quarterly rolling basis.</p>
<p>INE added that the number of jobless fell 0.89 percent from the previous month to 3.47 million.</p>
<p>The unemployment rate stands at 28.92 percent for women and at 17.08 percent for men.</p>
<p>The total number of employed rose 0.34 percent to 12.56 million.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
